  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Monday)\nIssued at 129 AM CDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nRidging will continue to exert its influence over the weekend, \nresulting in a rebound of temperatures. Interquartile ranges \nsuggest 90s to lower 100s (with the warmest temperatures farther \nsouth). Targeted heat advisories may be needed, but widespread \nadvisories look unlikely.\n\nThe ridge leaves room for a few shortwaves to ride around the \nperiphery, keeping 10-30% chances for rain in our area over the \nweekend. A few deterministic models depict an overnight MCS during\nthis time period.\n\nBeyond Sunday, confidence drops significantly. The interquartile\nspread for high temperatures increases to 15 to 25 degrees as\nmodels diverge on the potential approach of another cold front.\nWarmer solutions (due to stronger ridging) appear to be the more\nlikely scenario, but alternate scenarios (10-20% probability)\ncould bring substantial cooling (highs in the 70s and 80s\nareawide).\n\nDay",
